{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a stitch task (Task ID: 5636) from a code generation pipeline. The task requires implementing `cmd/vidir/main.go` - the vidir utility from moreutils. vidir allows batch renaming and deletion of files by editing a directory listing in a text editor. The implementation must follow srd114-vidir requirements R1.1 through R1.4 and R2.1-R2.2, adhere to strict coding standards from the execution constitution (40-line function limit, copyright headers, no scope creep, etc.), and pass compilation and vet checks.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **vidir** - moreutils utility for batch file rename/delete via text editor\n   - **SRD srd114-vidir** - Software Requirements Document defining vidir behavior\n   - **Differential testing** via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` against reference `vidir` binary (no g-prefix)\n   - **SIGPIPE handling** via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - **Cobbler scaffold pipeline** - automated code generation system (measure + stitch phases)\n   - **Execution constitution** - strict coding rules (E1-E10) including 40-line function limit, no git commands, write-all-then-build strategy\n   - **Go style constitution** - copyright headers, naming conventions, error handling patterns\n   - **Package contracts** for pkg/sys, pkg/testutils, pkg/format, etc.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd114-vidir.yaml** (READ)\n     - Defines the complete vidir specification\n     - R1.1: List files as \"NUMBER\\tFILENAME\", open in $EDITOR (default vi)\n     - R1.2: Parse editor output for renames/deletions\n     - R1.3: Process renames before deletions, create parent dirs\n     - R1.4: -v/--verbose prints actions to stderr\n     - R